# SS-20 - Separate date-range simulation and animated trades
Workstream ID: SS-20
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/StonksSniper/issues/20
Status: DONE
Milestone: M1.2
Dependencies: SS-03, SS-04, SS-05

## Purpose
Let a learner choose dates for the selected stock and idea, watch simulated
buys/sells and charts in a separate window, and see final INR/percentage P&L.

## Tasks
- [x] Add Simulate beside Test idea and open an independent non-modal window.
- [x] Capture the actual loaded history, strategy, starting money and costs.
- [x] Validate inclusive date bounds and run the existing causal accounting engine.
- [x] Animate price/trade/money prefixes with pause, stepping, restart and final result.
- [x] Show final INR and percentage gain/loss, including labelled marked holdings.
- [x] Stop owned timers on close and honor the main Animations switch.
- [x] Document warmup, loaded-data bounds, costs, holdings and release distinction.
- [x] Complete final regressions and document remaining delivery boundaries.

## Acceptance criteria
- Only actual loaded observations feed the application; no fabricated data or hidden fetch.
- Start/end are inclusive and bounded by loaded history; bad ranges fail explicitly.
- Warmup is inside the chosen interval, with initial cash and no pre-start position.
- Signals execute next available open; final signals cannot execute beyond the range.
- No future price, trade, equity or P&L appears during playback.
- Final monetary/percentage P&L includes charged costs and marked unsold holdings,
  without pretending marked returns are realized cash or charging invented final exits.
- Main edits leave the captured simulation independent; date edits clear stale output.
- Closing stops the window's timer; no user-owned process/window is driven or restarted.
- Technical verification is distinct from human/DPI acceptance or a new frozen release.

## Completion evidence
- All 12 date-range desktop regression cases passed. Final full offline suite:
  220 passed, 3 opt-in live tests skipped, with a normal process exit.
  Ruff lint/format, strict source mypy and Git whitespace checks passed.
- Owned offscreen actual-HDFCBANK check loaded 493 observations, retained the
  dated missing-row warning and exercised all 27 strategies over 444 observations
  from 2025-01-10 to 2026-10-27. Verified timer playback through the final SMA day.
- Inspected actual source-native price/money simulation views at 1160x768 and
  the main button layout at 1366x768. No user window was controlled.
- Independently checked profitable, losing, flat, cash-only and completed-sale
  results, including costs; invalid ranges cannot leave old results visible.
- Published v0.2.0 is unchanged and does not contain this source-only feature.
  Normal Windows/DPI interaction and human acceptance are not claimed verified.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-12: Implemented the requested date-range Simulate window using the
  existing engine, without changing strategy formulas, execution or accounting.
  Explicitly chose loaded-data bounds and in-range warmup; excluded all carry-in
  positions. Added persistent series and owned replay lifecycle, documented
  marked unsold holdings and preserved the published prototype.
- 2026-11-12: Final full regressions passed after updating the tracking inventory
  from 19 to 20 workstreams. Technical completion does not imply a new frozen
  executable release or human acceptance.
